Pick the first tied logit in the WebGPU argmax shader, matching CPU greedy.

llama.cpp's CPU greedy sampler keeps the first candidate when two logits are
equal (`>`). The WebGPU shader used `>=` in the local scan and the larger
index in the reduction, so a tie chose the later token. Ties are rare, but
they made GPU greedy disagree with CPU. Same-value comparisons now keep the
smaller index.

